v0.10.25: clean up test-fixture cruft, plug the leak

The v0.10.20/v0.10.24 legacy-slug tools surfaced 565 orphan
`test_agent_<uuid>` rows in the `agents` table — accumulated
over months from 6 leaking test fixtures in
agent-bestiary/memory/src/ that upsert but never clean up. The
rename tool preserves them; correct remedy is DELETE gated by
strong safety criteria. This release delivers both the cleanup
tool and the test-side leak fix.

Read side has been coping with `WHERE agent_name NOT LIKE
'test_agent_%'` in every listing endpoint. Fine as belt+braces
but the invariant should be "DB doesn't contain garbage" not
"every read remembers to filter garbage."

Changes:

  Migration 169 — CASCADE the mig-049 FKs on agents(agent_id)
  ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Every other FK on that column already declares ON DELETE
  CASCADE. The 4 in mig-049 (agent_alignments, pairwise_coherence,
  knowledge_transfers, agent_interaction_policies) didn't, which
  would block DELETE FROM agents. Semantically these should
  cascade — derived data is meaningless without the source.
  Idempotent, PgBouncer-safe, per-constraint EXCEPTION handlers.

  admin_cleanup_test_cruft_handler (src/handlers/admin.rs)
  ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Route: GET/POST /api/admin/agents/cleanup-test-cruft
  POST ?apply=true executes.

  Safety criteria (server-side, always enforced):
    * agent_name LIKE '<prefix>%'  (default test_agent_)
    * total_executions = 0         (never ran real work)
    * created_at older than grace  (default 24h)
    * tier NOT IN ('curated', 'system')

  Deliberately NOT gated on visibility/status: the leaking test
  fixtures set visibility='public' (either explicit factory or
  mig-010 default), so that gate would PROTECT the exact rows
  we want cleaned. The remaining 4 layers are enough defense.

  Every deletion → admin_bypass_events with full row snapshot.
  Audit INSERT before DELETE in same tx: trail can't outrun the
  action.

  CLI: abw admin agents cleanup-test-cruft
  ─────────────────────────────────────────
  Flags: --apply --prefix --older-than-hours --limit --json.
  Pretty table with compact preview (first 10 + last 5 for big
  batches). Truncation state + resume tip surfaced in summary.

  Test-side leak plugged
  ──────────────────────
  * locking.rs: 4 tests → all call cleanup_test_agent() at end
  * store.rs:   6 tests → all call cleanup_test_agent() at end
                also flipped test_agent() factory visibility from
                "public" to "private" — fixtures shouldn't pollute
                the catalogue regardless
  * consolidation.rs: 1 test → inline cleanup

  Panics still leak (Rust unwind skips post-panic cleanup) but
  the server-side handler sweeps those up on demand.

Suggested workflow:

  abw admin agents cleanup-test-cruft               # dry-run
  abw admin agents cleanup-test-cruft --limit 100 --apply
  # → repeat until: summary reports 0 matched.

Not in scope:
  - Drop-guard / macro-wrapped test cleanup for the panic case.
    v0.10.26 candidate (real infra work, not a hotfix).
  - Removing the read-side NOT LIKE filters. Left as defense
    until prod is proven clean.

Related:
  v0.10.20  legacy-slug rename tool (sibling for unroutable names)
  v0.10.23  perf fix (GIN + N+1→1) — made these tools usable
  v0.10.24  --prefix/--limit pattern applied here to cleanup
  v0.11.0   trust-contract would refuse deploy on non-zero
            test_agent count
